+### Duration
+
+{class}`Duration` accepts a whole number of seconds or a compact string of `<integer><unit>` groups and converts it to
+a {class}`datetime.timedelta`. The units are `d` (days), `h` (hours), `m` (minutes), and `s` (seconds). Each
+unit may appear at most once, in that order, without spaces. Units are case-insensitive. Valid values include `120`,
+`90m`, `1h30m`, and `1d2h3m4s`.
+
+```{eval-rst}
+.. click:example::
+
+    @click.command()
+    @click.option("--timeout", type=click.Duration(), default="30s")
+    def wait(timeout):
+        click.echo(f"timeout={timeout.total_seconds()}s")
+
+.. click:run::
+
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=1h30m'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=120'])
+    invoke(wait, args=['--timeout=30m1h'])
+```
+
